[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2484380326","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99145#issuecomment-2484380326","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99145","id":2484380326,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6UFKKm","user":{"login":"BastiaanOlij","id":1945449,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5NDU0NDk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1945449?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij","html_url":"https://github.com/BastiaanOlij","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-18T23:28:18Z","updated_at":"2024-11-18T23:28:18Z","body":"This feels very ugly to me and not something we'd want in the normal engine. I know people are going to abuse this and start giving us grief about it. There are plenty of people who don't understand the consequences of this and want this behaviour because they think that's how you do cut scenes or force a user to look in a given direction. Then start complaining about broken behaviour because it makes their users sick.\r\n\r\nFor a testing edge case, it feels wrong to add this in.\r\n\r\nThat said, I can't think of a good option to solve this nicely.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2484380326/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2485709670","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99145#issuecomment-2485709670","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99145","id":2485709670,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6UKOtm","user":{"login":"dsnopek","id":191561,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MTU2MQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/191561?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek","html_url":"https://github.com/dsnopek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-19T13:25:31Z","updated_at":"2024-11-19T13:33:27Z","body":"@BastiaanOlij Is there a way we could make the option sufficiently \"hidden\" that you'd be OK with it?\r\n\r\nBecause it is really useful! You can keep the headset on your desk, and run automated benchmarks or tests that report back via logs or a file, which can make for nice iteration.  (Note: on the Quest, you need to use the Developer Hub app or some `adb` commands to prevent the headset from going to sleep)\r\n\r\nImagine trying different changes to a scene (messing with materials, or number of objects, or something) and being able to quickly check if it improved performance without having to put the headset on and off.\r\n\r\n> This feels very ugly to me and not something we'd want in the normal engine.\r\n\r\nI think it needs to be in the normal engine (not just tools builds or something) so that folks can benchmark their game's scenes with a release build, which will naturally have different performance numbers.\r\n\r\n> There are plenty of people who don't understand the consequences of this and want this behaviour because they think that's how you do cut scenes or force a user to look in a given direction.\r\n\r\nI could understand how someone could have this misguided idea at first, but I feel like they'll realize how uncomfortable this is as soon as they tried it.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2485709670/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2486714960","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99145#issuecomment-2486714960","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99145","id":2486714960,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6UOEJQ","user":{"login":"BastiaanOlij","id":1945449,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5NDU0NDk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1945449?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij","html_url":"https://github.com/BastiaanOlij","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-19T20:44:18Z","updated_at":"2024-11-19T20:44:18Z","body":"@dsnopek like I said in my last line, I can't right now think of a better way so possibly we'll just have to accept this for the use case. As we discussed on RocketChat, I've had ideas for a long time on how I want to improve the camera system to make things far more flexible but those changes are far more invasive and possibly Godot 5.x territory.\r\n\r\nIt still feels icky to me but I can't argue with the ease of benchmarking enabled by this.\r\n\r\nI use developer hub alot, turning the proximity sensor off and using the casting feature is a perfect way to just have your headset sitting somewhere and running through iterations of testing.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2486714960/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":2,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2540272052","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99145#issuecomment-2540272052","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99145","id":2540272052,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6XaXm0","user":{"login":"BastiaanOlij","id":1945449,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5NDU0NDk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1945449?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij","html_url":"https://github.com/BastiaanOlij","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/followers","following_ur